_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_

**`useEffect` without deps re-executes every render**

The sticky-bottom effect is implemented as:

```ts
useEffect(() => {
  if (hitBottom) scrollChatToBottom();
});
```

With no dependency array React executes this effect on **every render**, even when neither `hitBottom` nor `renderMessages.length` changed, causing an unnecessary DOM read (`dom.scrollHeight`) and a forced layout on each paint cycle.

Attach a dependency list restricted to the reactive values that really matter (usually `hitBottom` and `renderMessages.length`):

```diff
-useEffect(() => {
-  if (hitBottom) scrollChatToBottom();
-});
+useEffect(() => {
+  if (hitBottom) scrollChatToBottom();
+}, [hitBottom, renderMessages.length]);
```

This keeps the sticky-bottom behaviour while avoiding gratuitous work on unrelated re-renders.

